From a4290eca7262e8966ccdd75b3d5b457f7e051f1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brennan Lamoreaux <brennan.lamoreaux@broadcom.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Aug 2025 17:47:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Canister GCC Plugins: Implement type check

Normalize the type name strings that are obtained
from either the GCC representation or the DWARF debuginfo
so that they match up and can be used for comparison.

Implement the type comparison check as a recursive loop
for each structure, following the chain of data structures.
Throws error if the type doesn't match between kernel and
canister versions.

To account for unions, changed the structures to be more generic
data structures and data members.

Added a new structure field which can point to definitions of other
data structures, either internal or external structs/unions. This
can be traversed recursively to fully compare structure definitions.

Generally have an exception for "void *", where we allow replacing
any other pointer with "void *".

To specify accepted/vetted differences between the kernel and
canister fields, added a new attribute "canister_mismatch",
which can be specified like:
__attribute__((canister_mismatch(KERN_TYPE, CANISTER_TYPE)))

Other enhancements:
1. make clean - removes canister_structures.db
2. Ignore canister_structures.db from git index
3. Changed size of padding field in matching plugin to match
   only to the end of the last canister field, instead of
   padding to match the entire canister structure size.
4. Implement iterators on both canister debuginfo and GCC
   sides for stepping through data structures.
5. Shrink cache by 3-4x by properly remapping data structures,
   and keeping only unique.

Signed-off-by: Brennan Lamoreaux <brennan.lamoreaux@broadcom.com>
